<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Landgraviate of Hesse-Rheinfels</h1><p class="st-meta">1567 CE – 1583 CE · capital St. Goar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived Hessian landgraviate on the middle Rhine, ruled by Philip II from Rheinfels castle above St. Goar.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the 1567 division of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/landgraviate-of-hesse">Landgraviate of Hesse</a> among the sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-i-landgrave-of-hesse">Philip the Magnanimous</a>, the third son, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-landgrave-of-hesse-rheinfels">Philip II</a>, received the Lower <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-katzenelnbogen">County of Katzenelnbogen</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rheinfels-castle">Rheinfels</a> castle above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sankt-goar">St. Goar</a> as his residence.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-landgrave-of-hesse-rheinfels">Philip II</a> rebuilt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rheinfels-castle">Rheinfels</a> as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> residence and fortress, controlling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> tolls at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sankt-goar">St. Goar</a> that were the territory's main income. His small state was Lutheran, like its Hessian neighbours. He married Anna <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elisabeth-of-the-palatinate">Elisabeth of the Palatinate</a> but had no children.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-landgrave-of-hesse-rheinfels">Philip II</a> died in 1583, his lands were divided among his brothers, most going to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/landgraviate-of-hesse-kassel">Landgraviate of Hesse-Kassel</a>, with smaller shares to Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marburg">Marburg</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-hesse">Hesse-Darmstadt</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rheinfels-castle">Rheinfels</a> became one of the largest castles on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> before French troops blew it up in 1797.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/landgraviate-of-hesse-rheinfels.jpg" alt="Landgraviate of Hesse-Rheinfels" width="320" height="420"><figcaption>Image: Marion Halft · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hessen-Rheinfels_Coat_of_arms.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1567 CE – 1583 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>St. Goar</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Philip II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hessen-Rheinfels</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1575&amp;focus=landgraviate-of-hesse-rheinfels" aria-label="Landgraviate of Hesse-Rheinfels on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4876 405 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Landgraviate of Hesse-Rheinfels lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5196 661L5215 656"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5215 656h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5196 661h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5196 661h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks St. Goar. <a href="/atlas?year=1575&amp;focus=landgraviate-of-hesse-rheinfels">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
